{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791561866,"nonce":"tHEY78qKLk0IQprYag10Q5Dmn58=","title":"Loop-free float functions round unfused in the interpreter and fused once compiled","message":"18381a5 (\"Prepare interpreter SSA only for loop bodies\") runs a loop-free function from decoded bytecode instead of its AIR body. AIR is where multiply-adds are fused (FmaPeephole), and the compiled tiers run AIR, so such a function rounded a*b+c twice while interpreted and once after promotion. A call made before promotion and the same call after it could differ in the last bit, and --mode interp disagreed with --mode jit.\n\nFound by ChimpMonk's humanoid push-recovery check (chimpmonk git-bug e63a008): the same shove under even and uneven frame times must give identical results, and promotion landing at different points of the two runs changed them (\"uneven frames changed the push at 90 degrees\"; --jit-tier llvm: \"the fall at 180 degrees was not clean\"). v0.1.5 passes; 781ebbb fails; ASH_AIR_ALL=1 or --no-fma passes.\n\nMinimal reproducer (crates/ash/test/tests/TestFmaPromotionParity.hx): mulAdd(0.1, 10, -1) called before and after promotion. Broken hybrid: before=0 after=5.55111512312578e-17; broken --mode interp: 0 while --mode jit gives 5.55e-17.","files":null}]}